THE REMAINING DIVERGENCE, A POLICY RATHER THAN A DEFECT THIS SLICE FIXES ALONE.

The 31 T-dec-* vectors: malformed UTF-8 in a string field, which
CONTRACT.md says a conformant parser must reject. This build accepts
them, because it reads strings through Encoding.UTF8, which SUBSTITUTES
U+FFFD. Google.Protobuf does the same (`harness utf8`). The rejecting
policy is the separate /p:AkStrict=true build (ABI v1 open decision 3).

U-map-entry, which earlier runs listed here, is a DISPUTED row in the corpus
now and is reported in the disputed section above, outside pass/fail.

C5 (produce) and the chunking class, stated rather than claimed:
  * C5 asks a slice to BUILD each message from the description and encode
    it. This slice has payload builders for `ffi/schema`'s roots only, and
    `harness conformance` is that claim: byte identity on all 16 payloads.
    For the corpus's own roots there is no builder, so C3 (re-encode what
    was parsed) is what runs and C5 is NOT claimed for them.
